# Makefile.uk: which source files are compiled into the image.  *** YOU IMPLEMENT ***
#
# This is what makes runner.c, and your own library, part of the unikernel.
# Both are compiled INTO the image from source, the same way as any Unikraft
# library.
#
# See SPEC.md Part I (TODO A) and Part III (TODO B).
#
# TODO(student) A: register this application and add runner.c.
#
#     $(eval $(call addlib,apprunner))
#
#   The name you pass defines the variables you use next: `apprunner` gives you
#   APPRUNNER_BASE (this directory) and APPRUNNER_SRCS-y (its sources).
#
#   runner.c is NOT in this directory and must NOT be copied here: it is in
#   runner/, one level up. Express its path relative to APPRUNNER_BASE:
#
#     APPRUNNER_SRCS-y += $(APPRUNNER_BASE)/../runner/runner.c
#
# TODO(student) B (SPEC Part III): register your statistics library as a SECOND
#   library.
#
#   Registering it with addlib makes it a separate library in the build, so its
#   source is only compiled when the Config.uk option you declared is true:
#
#     $(eval $(call addlib,libukstats))
#     LIBUKSTATS_BASE := $(APPRUNNER_BASE)/libukstats
#     LIBUKSTATS_SRCS-$(CONFIG_APPRUNNER_STATS) += $(LIBUKSTATS_BASE)/ukstats.c
#
#   The `-$(CONFIG_APPRUNNER_STATS)` suffix is what makes ukstats.c compile only
#   when that option is true.
#
# As shipped this file registers nothing, so the build produces no application
# code and the image will not serve anything.
